  "format": "JPEG or PNG, equirectangular. Bodies: east longitude from -180 at the left to 180 at the right, 0 at the centre, north at the top (planetocentric). Milky Way: galactic coordinates, longitude 0 at the centre increasing to the left, the south galactic pole at the top. Saturn's rings: a radial strip from the inner edge of the C ring to the outer edge of the A ring, with transparency. The Moon, Mars and Mercury also name a tile service (WMTS, equirectangular) for detail at close range.",
  "coverage": "The Sun, Mercury, Venus (its clouds), the Moon, Mars, Jupiter, Saturn and its rings, Uranus, Neptune; the whole sky",
